WEBVTT

00:00:01.710 --> 00:00:07.000
It possesses enormous power,
and brings endless pleasure

00:00:07.090 --> 00:00:10.960
and destruction  to those who are destined.

00:00:11.050 --> 00:00:12.720
The Witchblade.

00:00:12.800 --> 00:00:15.800
At this moment, one woman has awakened.

00:00:29.770 --> 00:00:33.460
Just before the shot, my chest feels like it's gonna tear open

00:00:33.640 --> 00:00:37.050
I shout out countless times, break out

00:00:37.190 --> 00:00:42.240
It's not over, rush through the endless night

00:00:43.950 --> 00:00:47.530
Hot blood flows through my body

00:00:47.850 --> 00:00:51.240
The moment it ultimately rots away

00:00:51.300 --> 00:00:57.840
it's all over, fragments of an empty dream come to mind

00:00:58.310 --> 00:01:03.340
I can never go back, I can't remember a thing

00:01:05.440 --> 00:01:08.880
I've been reduced to struggling, and my voice won't carry

00:01:09.020 --> 00:01:12.390
Uncontrollable impulses

00:01:12.410 --> 00:01:19.310
Give me your XTC, let me feel it one more time

00:01:19.320 --> 00:01:26.530
This body heats up, and I shout out your name in the darkness

00:01:26.580 --> 00:01:33.530
Give me your XTC, I don't need false love

00:01:33.550 --> 00:01:36.710
I will accept it, sin and punishment

00:01:36.820 --> 00:01:43.280
Slash through the destiny I've been set up with, Blade

00:01:46.640 --> 00:01:51.900
"Sadness"

00:02:20.390 --> 00:02:22.140
W-What?

00:02:22.220 --> 00:02:24.470
I have a request...

00:02:24.560 --> 00:02:31.900
Please say, "I wish upon a star
that my love reaches you..."

00:02:32.900 --> 00:02:36.150
Please. Please say it.

00:02:37.990 --> 00:02:44.870
Please say it. "I wish upon a star
that my love reaches you..."

00:02:44.950 --> 00:02:48.750
W-What is this?! Are you crazy or something?!

00:02:52.460 --> 00:02:55.960
Please. Hurry...

00:02:59.220 --> 00:03:00.420
...and say it!

00:03:19.440 --> 00:03:23.450
No more! I... I...

00:03:31.210 --> 00:03:34.830
Dammit! That's three days in a row now!

00:03:34.920 --> 00:03:40.300
And this time, they're all
young women unrelated to the NSWF...

00:03:40.380 --> 00:03:42.380
Just what the hell's goin' on?!

00:03:43.970 --> 00:03:45.840
Yeah, seriously...

00:03:48.930 --> 00:03:50.640
Hey, you!

00:03:50.730 --> 00:03:53.730
You again?! Gimme a break already,
you damn hyena!

00:03:53.810 --> 00:03:55.810
Whoopsies!

00:03:55.900 --> 00:03:59.320
If you want someone to blame,
you should blame the killer.

00:03:59.400 --> 00:04:02.570
And your own incompetent self!

00:04:02.650 --> 00:04:04.910
D-Damn you!

00:04:07.450 --> 00:04:10.160
Alright! Another toast!

00:04:10.250 --> 00:04:11.700
Cheers!

00:04:14.790 --> 00:04:19.880
You sure know how to drink, Masamune-Chan!

00:04:21.210 --> 00:04:24.130
Hey, Tozawa! Come drink with us!

00:04:24.220 --> 00:04:26.340
We're celebrating, Tozawa-Chan!

00:04:26.430 --> 00:04:30.310
Michael got his first job since moving in!

00:04:30.390 --> 00:04:32.980
A job? Doing what?

00:04:35.400 --> 00:04:40.770
I can see it... a black
shadow above Michael's head...

00:04:40.860 --> 00:04:45.780
I think I'll pass for today.
I'm really busy with stuff lately...

00:04:46.990 --> 00:04:50.780
You tryin' to run out on me?!
R-Run out?

00:04:50.870 --> 00:04:55.870
You hired me to do a job, remember?
What's the story with that?

00:04:55.960 --> 00:04:59.130
No, it's not really anything that

00:04:59.210 --> 00:05:05.300
Oh, I get it! You're scared now that
you've seen me looking like that!

00:05:07.680 --> 00:05:09.720
M-Me, scared?!

00:05:09.800 --> 00:05:12.260
Wait! Looking like what?!
Did you seem 'em pop out?!

00:05:12.350 --> 00:05:14.020
Wanna see, wanna see?!

00:05:14.100 --> 00:05:17.140
Okay, then I'll show ya!

00:05:19.650 --> 00:05:22.230
H-Hey, quit it, Masamune!

00:05:22.320 --> 00:05:25.740
Are you still drinking, Mom?!

00:05:25.820 --> 00:05:28.910
You should really stop, you know...

00:05:34.250 --> 00:05:35.750
Mom!

00:05:35.830 --> 00:05:38.170
Say, what did you see her looking like?

00:05:38.250 --> 00:05:41.340
Oh... Like this.

00:05:41.420 --> 00:05:43.300
Oh, I see...

00:05:47.800 --> 00:05:50.840
Want some water, Mom?

00:05:50.930 --> 00:05:52.760
No, thanks...

00:05:52.850 --> 00:05:55.850
Riko... Gimme a kiss...

00:05:55.930 --> 00:05:58.600
Sheesh, you're so hopeless...

00:06:05.360 --> 00:06:10.860
Tell your mom that we
start work again tomorrow.

00:06:10.950 --> 00:06:15.700
All right. But only
because she's working for you.

00:06:15.790 --> 00:06:17.870
You're so suspicious, Tozawa-Chan.

00:06:17.960 --> 00:06:19.040
Yeah, right.

00:06:22.250 --> 00:06:24.840
Look, look! It's a whale!

00:06:32.890 --> 00:06:34.850
It's Mr. Whale!

00:06:38.350 --> 00:06:41.650
Oh, no! Are you all right?!

00:06:42.860 --> 00:06:45.730
It's okay now. Don't cry.

00:06:46.940 --> 00:06:51.030
Excuse me... More coffee, please...

00:06:51.110 --> 00:06:53.200
Certainly!

00:06:53.280 --> 00:06:54.780
My head hurts...

00:06:54.870 --> 00:07:00.790
That's your fifteenth cup, you know.
Are you even listening to me?

00:07:00.870 --> 00:07:04.670
I am! So, what again?

00:07:04.750 --> 00:07:09.840
We're talking about those incidents.
There've been three victims now.

00:07:09.920 --> 00:07:15.350
The second one had a guy with her.
But he was left unscathed...

00:07:15.430 --> 00:07:18.270
Which means we have a witness.

00:07:20.180 --> 00:07:22.890
The killer is probably...

00:07:22.980 --> 00:07:27.820
Yeah, that's what we're gonna check now.

00:07:27.900 --> 00:07:35.660
What was it that I sensed then?

00:07:42.330 --> 00:07:47.000
How is it? I tried whipping
up my own white sauce...

00:07:47.090 --> 00:07:52.380
Mmm! It's delish! My cheeks
are just gonna fall right off!

00:07:52.470 --> 00:07:55.760
There's still a lot left, so have all you want!

00:07:57.390 --> 00:07:59.180
Something the matter, Rihoko-Chan?

00:07:59.270 --> 00:08:02.810
It's discount time at the
supermarket! I gotta go!

00:08:04.190 --> 00:08:08.650
1 1 :45? You're absolutely sure?

00:08:08.730 --> 00:08:14.400
Yes. I checked my watch to see
when the late-night bus would come.

00:08:14.490 --> 00:08:15.450
And then...

00:08:15.530 --> 00:08:18.910
You saw the killer's face, didn't you?

00:08:18.990 --> 00:08:23.870
Yes... I'll never be
able to forget that face...

00:08:23.960 --> 00:08:27.580
Please, say it.

00:08:27.670 --> 00:08:33.420
"I wish upon a star that
my love reaches you..."

00:08:36.640 --> 00:08:40.850
He's not human! He's... not human!

00:08:46.190 --> 00:08:52.230
What does, "I wish upon a star
that my love reaches you," mean?

00:08:52.320 --> 00:08:56.700
No clue. And there's one
other thing that bugs me...

00:08:56.780 --> 00:08:57.780
What's that?

00:08:57.870 --> 00:09:02.160
The time of the incident... 1 1 :45.

00:09:02.250 --> 00:09:05.620
All three of 'em were killed at that time...

00:09:05.710 --> 00:09:07.000
What do you think?

00:09:07.080 --> 00:09:10.500
Yeah... Could it just be coincidence?

00:09:17.550 --> 00:09:19.680
Oh! Paprika is cheap!

00:09:30.900 --> 00:09:33.650
Umm, we certainly meet often...

00:09:38.070 --> 00:09:40.740
Do you...

00:09:40.830 --> 00:09:44.830
Do you always go shopping alone?
Where's your mother?

00:09:44.910 --> 00:09:48.830
Oh, she's sort of busy with work...

00:09:48.920 --> 00:09:53.130
Oh. Do you like your mother?
Yeah!

00:09:53.210 --> 00:09:55.170
In what way?

00:09:55.260 --> 00:09:59.300
What do you mean? We're family!

00:10:01.680 --> 00:10:05.310
Umm, this is my street...

00:10:05.390 --> 00:10:07.850
I'll see you later, then.
Bye!

00:10:22.240 --> 00:10:23.990
Thank you!

00:10:29.920 --> 00:10:31.170
What's this?!

00:10:31.250 --> 00:10:32.880
Wait!

00:10:35.800 --> 00:10:40.590
I've never experienced this before...

00:10:45.390 --> 00:10:46.720
What is this?

00:10:48.060 --> 00:10:51.980
Umm, is something the matter?

00:10:52.060 --> 00:10:55.270
It's incredible... But...

00:10:58.780 --> 00:11:03.910
Would you like one?

00:11:04.950 --> 00:11:06.580
What's up?

00:11:06.660 --> 00:11:08.830
No, it's nothing...

00:11:20.880 --> 00:11:24.970
Do you always eat this kind of stuff, Mister?

00:11:26.010 --> 00:11:28.010
Yes. Why do you ask?

00:11:28.100 --> 00:11:31.270
Don't you have a girlfriend or
someone who can make you lunches?

00:11:31.350 --> 00:11:37.190
Oh, I do have a girlfriend,
but I hardly get to see her...

00:11:37.270 --> 00:11:43.740
I'm thinking about buying a house now,
so we can live together.

00:11:43.820 --> 00:11:49.040
That way, she won't
have to be lonely anymore...

00:11:49.120 --> 00:11:56.840
A house, huh? I hope my mom
and I can get one too, someday!

00:11:56.920 --> 00:12:00.380
Say, what kind of house do you want?

00:12:05.930 --> 00:12:09.390
A big living room with a wooden floor...

00:12:09.470 --> 00:12:15.400
With a fireplace here, for us
to relax in front of after dinner...

00:12:15.480 --> 00:12:19.770
You must really like your girlfriend a lot...

00:12:20.940 --> 00:12:26.870
I sure do. She's the prettiest
and kindest girl in the whole world.

00:12:26.950 --> 00:12:29.660
There's no one greater than her.

00:12:32.620 --> 00:12:37.290
My break time is over.
I need to get back to work now.

00:12:38.920 --> 00:12:40.960
Will you be here tomorrow, Mister?

00:12:41.050 --> 00:12:43.420
Yes, I come every afternoon.

00:12:43.510 --> 00:12:47.260
In that case, I'll make you a lunch!

00:12:47.340 --> 00:12:49.720
Thank you!

00:12:49.810 --> 00:12:55.640
Why do you ignore our repeated
requests for progress reports?

00:12:55.730 --> 00:12:59.690
I would really like to
know, Director Takayama...

00:12:59.770 --> 00:13:03.230
The Special Section's
work is just that... special.

00:13:03.320 --> 00:13:06.950
I'd like you to understand that it's
to protect secrets from being leaked.

00:13:07.030 --> 00:13:11.240
And I'd like to pray that
that's not a convenient excuse,

00:13:11.330 --> 00:13:15.960
but if your section can't produce results,
then it's just a money pit

00:13:16.040 --> 00:13:19.210
whose very existence must be questioned.

00:13:19.290 --> 00:13:21.670
Are things really all right?

00:13:21.750 --> 00:13:26.760
It's no exaggeration that the company's
future rests on the Witchblade.

00:13:26.840 --> 00:13:29.340
Let me put it this way.

00:13:29.430 --> 00:13:34.140
We've discovered a treasure chest.
Now we simply need to open it...

00:13:34.230 --> 00:13:37.600
Why can't you be any more specific?

00:13:37.690 --> 00:13:40.650
I haven't looked inside
the treasure chest just yet,

00:13:40.730 --> 00:13:44.690
so I wouldn't want to possibly
disappoint you gentlemen.

00:13:44.780 --> 00:13:47.700
Another excuse, huh?

00:13:47.780 --> 00:13:51.530
I apologize for referring to personal matters,

00:13:51.620 --> 00:13:55.120
but when Takayama-kun and I
were in the rowing club in college,

00:13:55.200 --> 00:14:02.420
he rowed in the position behind me,
staring at my back all the while.

00:14:02.500 --> 00:14:07.130
Wadou-san, rowing is done facing backwards.

00:14:07.220 --> 00:14:11.390
In other words, I was closer
to the goal than you were.

00:14:16.020 --> 00:14:18.810
I was referring to rowing.
There is no deeper meaning.

00:14:21.190 --> 00:14:26.280
All the murders have taken place
in the vicinity of this radio station.

00:14:26.360 --> 00:14:30.450
And they all happened at 1 1 :45...

00:14:30.530 --> 00:14:34.780
Assuming they're not coincidences,
we should see him soon...

00:14:34.870 --> 00:14:35.950
Yes...

00:14:40.620 --> 00:14:41.750
M-Masamune!

00:14:41.830 --> 00:14:45.710
W-What the ?! What are you?!

00:14:45.800 --> 00:14:49.420
Please, say it...

00:14:49.510 --> 00:14:54.800
"I wish upon a star that
my love reaches you..."

00:15:02.940 --> 00:15:04.400
Run! Hurry!

00:15:18.120 --> 00:15:24.130
If this guy's involved,
there's gotta be info on him here!

00:15:24.210 --> 00:15:28.550
But are you sure it's okay for us
to be checking the police databanks?

00:15:33.090 --> 00:15:33.510
"Tragedy Strikes!
Model Officer Dies After Being Shot"

00:15:37.060 --> 00:15:38.600
...and was a policeman?!

00:15:38.680 --> 00:15:40.980
It's dated the year before the Great Quake...

00:15:41.060 --> 00:15:42.980
Damn you, Tozawa!

00:15:43.060 --> 00:15:48.270
You got guts, waltzing right
into police hands on your own!

00:15:48.360 --> 00:15:50.820
Come to get your ass kicked?

00:15:50.900 --> 00:15:55.990
H-Hold on, now! This place is
open to the general public!

00:15:56.080 --> 00:16:01.450
"General public" refers to honest,
upright citizens! But in your case

00:16:03.870 --> 00:16:06.710
T-That's Muraki...

00:16:06.790 --> 00:16:07.840
Muraki?

00:16:07.920 --> 00:16:10.460
B-Bastard! What's the meaning of this?!

00:16:10.550 --> 00:16:15.720
What do you mean? He's the guy
behind the string of murders...

00:16:15.800 --> 00:16:20.810
Like hell he is! What scheme are you
cooking up?! Tell me this instant!

00:16:20.890 --> 00:16:24.350
H-Hey, now! There's no
need to freak out like that!

00:16:28.190 --> 00:16:30.690
And this is the kitchen...

00:16:30.780 --> 00:16:36.820
It was her special request.
She's a very good cook, you know...

00:16:38.200 --> 00:16:40.990
Who makes better lunches, me or her?

00:16:41.080 --> 00:16:45.620
Oh, good question.
You're about the same, I guess?

00:16:46.750 --> 00:16:50.000
Whoops, I better get back to work.

00:16:50.090 --> 00:16:53.590
So I'll make another lunch for you tomorrow!

00:16:53.670 --> 00:16:56.800
After all, you still
haven't finished your house!

00:16:59.430 --> 00:17:02.180
How is that possible?

00:17:02.270 --> 00:17:05.850
Someone who's dead, killing people...

00:17:05.940 --> 00:17:08.400
Maybe it's just an uncanny look-alike?

00:17:11.070 --> 00:17:11.980
Mom!

00:17:12.070 --> 00:17:12.860
Riko!

00:17:12.940 --> 00:17:16.150
Guess what, guess what! I made a friend, too!

00:17:16.240 --> 00:17:18.700
Really?! What's the kid like?

00:17:20.240 --> 00:17:26.370
I wouldn't exactly call him
a "kid," but he's really nice!

00:17:26.460 --> 00:17:28.880
Introduce me to him sometime!
Okay!

00:17:28.960 --> 00:17:32.550
So, is work going okay for you, Mom?

00:17:32.630 --> 00:17:38.300
Not at all. We have lots
of possible hints, though...

00:17:38.390 --> 00:17:44.020
Like, "I wish upon a star,"
and, "May my love reach you..."

00:17:44.100 --> 00:17:46.020
Oh! That brings back memories!

00:17:46.100 --> 00:17:48.270
That's "Sakura's Twinkle Date"!

00:17:48.350 --> 00:17:52.230
I always tuned in to that
radio show! I was a huge fan!

00:17:52.320 --> 00:17:53.520
Radio?

00:17:53.610 --> 00:17:58.780
I was glued to the radio
every night at 1 1 :45! S-A-K-U-R

00:17:58.860 --> 00:18:01.410
1 1 :45?

00:18:06.870 --> 00:18:08.370
Detective Nakata!

00:18:11.210 --> 00:18:16.550
I'm sorry I got worked up earlier,
but what you're doing is pointless.

00:18:16.630 --> 00:18:17.970
Whaddya talkin' about?

00:18:18.050 --> 00:18:21.890
Don't play dumb! I know what you're after!

00:18:21.970 --> 00:18:25.180
I know you're tryin' to
expose the police cover-up!

00:18:25.270 --> 00:18:30.730
But nobody'll take the bait!
It's an old and trivial story, anyways.

00:18:30.810 --> 00:18:31.690
Huh?

00:18:31.770 --> 00:18:35.730
I'm askin' you to let it go.

00:18:35.820 --> 00:18:41.860
Muraki was one of my men.
He was serious to a fault.

00:18:41.950 --> 00:18:44.700
Which is why he committed suicide,

00:18:44.790 --> 00:18:48.660
but by calling it an honorable death,
his honor can be preserved...

00:18:48.750 --> 00:18:51.370
S-Suicide?! For reals?!

00:18:51.460 --> 00:18:53.790
I told you not to play dumb!

00:18:53.880 --> 00:18:57.760
Umm, was Muraki-san a fan of a radio show

00:18:57.840 --> 00:18:59.970
called Sakura's Twinkle Date or something?!

00:19:00.050 --> 00:19:04.010
See, you've already found out that much!

00:19:04.100 --> 00:19:10.430
Muraki tried to protect some DJ
named Sakura from a dangerous fan.

00:19:10.520 --> 00:19:15.690
But that backfired, and he wound
up being sued for stalking her...

00:19:15.770 --> 00:19:17.400
And that's when he...

00:19:22.950 --> 00:19:27.870
You can guess the rest.
He was serious to a fault.

00:19:27.950 --> 00:19:31.960
And the Sakura girl was killed
in the Great Quake afterwards...

00:19:34.710 --> 00:19:38.960
There's no question about it,
judging from the circumstances.

00:19:39.050 --> 00:19:43.970
The guy behind these murders
is Muraki, a former police officer.

00:19:44.050 --> 00:19:47.560
But why is someone who's dead...

00:19:47.640 --> 00:19:52.020
Yeah. There must be one helluva
secret being kept under wraps.

00:19:52.100 --> 00:19:55.770
In any case, our best bet now is
to confirm it with Muraki himself.

00:19:59.480 --> 00:20:02.570
No... No more...

00:20:02.650 --> 00:20:05.030
No more of this!

00:20:11.960 --> 00:20:13.120
There he is!

00:20:28.810 --> 00:20:32.180
What are you?! What are you doing here?!

00:20:32.270 --> 00:20:35.310
I shouldn't have come back to life!

00:20:36.650 --> 00:20:38.690
Please free me!

00:20:38.770 --> 00:20:42.280
Please destroy this cursed body!

00:20:42.360 --> 00:20:45.820
Hold on! Is that...

00:20:45.910 --> 00:20:47.910
...what I'm...

00:21:01.800 --> 00:21:06.180
Just what are X-Cons?

00:21:13.810 --> 00:21:17.650
He sure is late...
Riko.

00:21:17.730 --> 00:21:21.820
Mom!
What's wrong? Where's your friend?

00:21:21.900 --> 00:21:25.150
I don't know. I guess he can't come today.

00:21:25.240 --> 00:21:27.990
He must be really busy with work...

00:21:28.070 --> 00:21:32.870
Oh. Then let's go home together.

00:21:32.950 --> 00:21:34.000
Okay.

00:21:57.190 --> 00:22:07.280
I murmur, "I love you," with all my emotion

00:22:07.360 --> 00:22:16.620
All my feelings until yesterday now overflow and dissolve quickly

00:22:18.080 --> 00:22:28.550
If only this one last prayer could make it through...

00:22:28.630 --> 00:22:37.390
Thank you for giving us the words to ascertain each other, God

00:22:39.060 --> 00:22:49.400
Tomorrow, we'll reach out and hold hands harder than normal

00:22:49.490 --> 00:23:02.420
Tomorrow, we'll reach out, hug, kiss, and love each other

00:23:11.930 --> 00:23:13.260
What do I do?!

00:23:13.350 --> 00:23:16.010
I suddenly have to go to a party!

00:23:16.100 --> 00:23:19.850
With Takayama, of all people! Blech!

00:23:19.940 --> 00:23:24.560
It's probably just some boring
party full of high-class snobs.

00:23:24.650 --> 00:23:26.860
I'm not good at stuff like that.

00:23:26.940 --> 00:23:30.530
I don't know anything about making small-talk!

00:23:30.610 --> 00:23:35.030
Drinking with everyone at
Mariko-san's shop is way more fun!

00:23:35.120 --> 00:23:37.700
Man, I wanna go home!

00:23:37.790 --> 00:23:39.950
Let's hit the baths when I get home, okay?
